# Azure Speech — needed only to BAKE narration audio of your own.
#
# You do not need this to hear a deck. The trailer's audio is committed under
# public/voices/ and plays with nothing configured and no server running. This
# key is for the other direction: writing a new deck, or changing the words in
# an existing one, and generating fresh audio for it.
#
# Get a key: Azure Portal -> create a "Speech" resource -> Keys and Endpoint.
#
# Copy this file to .env, fill in your values, then:
#   npm run dev:server                          # the narrate server, port 5175
#   npm run bake -- <deckId>                    # writes public/voices/<deckId>/
#
# `npm run dev` starts the Vite dev server and the narrate server together.
# See README.md, "Narration: baked audio is the demo, the endpoint is the
# product".
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=...
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=eastus
